# Terminal-Based Pokémon Game (C/C++)

A terminal-based Pokémon-style game built in C/C++ using ncurses. The game features real-time map navigation, procedurally generated worlds, and NPCs with pathfinding AI.

---

## Features

- Procedurally generated world using seed-based randomization
- Real-time player movement and map rendering with ncurses
- NPCs with pathfinding AI that navigate terrain dynamically
- Multiple terrain types affecting movement behavior
- Encounter system (e.g., random Pokémon encounters in grass)
- Interactive locations such as Poké Marts and Centers

---

## Technical Highlights

- Implemented pathfinding logic for NPC movement across a dynamic grid
- Designed a tile-based map system with different terrain costs
- Built real-time rendering loop using ncurses for smooth terminal updates
- Used modular C/C++ design to separate game logic, rendering, and input handling

---

## Tech Stack

- Language: C / C++
- Libraries: ncurses
- Concepts: Pathfinding, Procedural Generation, Game Loops, Data Structures

## Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
- GCC / G++
- ncurses library

### Install ncurses (if needed)

Mac (Homebrew):
```bash
brew install ncurses

### Build and Run
make
./pokemon_game
